   <text:h text:outline-level="1">Putting it all together</text:h>
   <text:p>Don’t go around saying<text:change text:change-id="ct4"/> the world owes you a living.</text:p>
   <text:p>I really love <text:change text:change-id="ct1"/><text:change-start text:change-id="ct2"/>font-styles<text:change-end text:change-id="ct2"/>.</text:p>
   <text:p>To find <text:change-start text:change-id="ct3"/><text:span text:style-name="B">any</text:span> <text:change-end text:change-id="ct3"/>sense in any copyright law.</text:p>
   <text:p><office:annotation office:name="c1"><dc:creator>Bill Winter</dc:creator><dc:date>2024-04-08T10:32:00</dc:date><text:p>true</text:p></office:annotation>Truth is stranger than fiction<office:annotation-end office:name="c1"/>, but it is because Fiction is obliged to stick to possibilities.</text:p>
   <text:p><text:change text:change-id="ct5"/>The paragraph after the cut.</text:p>
   <text:p>One sentence,<text:change-start text:change-id="ct6"/></text:p>
   <text:p><text:change-end text:change-id="ct6"/>split in two.</text:p>
   <text:p>Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet.<office:annotation><dc:creator>Ana Lima</dc:creator><dc:date>2026-09-30T08:15:00</dc:date><text:p>This is a comment</text:p></office:annotation></text:p>
